{%- comment -%}
  Resolve a scent's swatch colour from a variant option value.

  Option values carry status suffixes that the palette metaobjects do not always
  mirror — 「淨心棉花（預購）」 on the product against 「淨心棉花」 in the palette, or the
  other way round. An exact string compare fails silently when the two drift
  apart, and because every lookup then lands on the same fallback, all six
  swatches collapse to one beige and the picker looks broken rather than stale.

  Compare on the part before the first bracket instead — full-width （ and
  half-width ( both — so renaming on either side no longer needs a code change.

  Accepts:
    name — the option value, e.g. '淨心棉花（預購）'

  Usage:
    {%- capture swatch_color -%}{%- render 'apgo-scent-hex', name: value -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign swatch_color = swatch_color | strip -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign wanted = name | split: '（' | first | split: '(' | first | strip
  assign out = ''

  assign palette = shop.metafields.apgo.scents.value
  if palette != blank
    for s in palette
      assign candidate = s.name | split: '（' | first | split: '(' | first | strip
      if candidate == wanted
        assign out = s.hex
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  # Safety net for when the shop metafield loses an entry. Keyed on the
  # bracket-stripped name for the same reason as the lookup above.
  if out == blank
    case wanted
      when '淨心棉花'
        assign out = '#E8DFC9'
      when '花漾蒼蘭'
        assign out = '#D4DDE0'
      when '浪漫玫瑰'
        assign out = '#E8D4CF'
      when '海洋晨曦'
        assign out = '#C8D6DA'
      when '清雅白茶'
        assign out = '#DAE0CE'
      when '薰衣紫戀'
        assign out = '#D6CFDD'
      else
        assign out = '#E8DFC9'
    endcase
  endif

  echo out
-%}
